From 1f423cbe556d3b5c7cd8ee7aef6770e41da3df4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:05:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] M10: subtitles: what is said, at the bottom of the screen,
 under who says it

GDD 16.6, with 17.1, 17.3 and 3.6. A CanvasLayer "Subtitles" in drive.tscn
(src/view/subtitles_view.gd, SubtitlesView) listens to `line_requested` on
the Events bus and shows that line of the line table at the bottom centre:
the speaker's name over at most two lines of 42 characters, held for the
larger of 1.5 s and 0.06 s per character. A line asked for while another
is showing waits its turn.

- The wrapping, the timing and the queue are a pure class, SubtitleQueue
  (src/view/subtitle_queue.gd). A text is cut at its spaces; two lines are
  cut where they are most alike; a text of more than two lines is shown in
  parts, each held for the time its own length asks for. A subtitle's time
  begins with the frame it is first drawn in, so it is never held less.
- A row that holds an exchange ("Guest, then Abu Noor" says "... / ...")
  is shown as what each of them says, one after the other, each under
  their own name.
- Speaker names are lines themselves: `speaker.` and the name in lower
  case with underscores (Lines.get_speaker_name). Nine are added to both
  line files; a speaker with no line is shown as the column has it.
- The labels' text direction is automatic. Arabic was looked at with a
  line table made in memory (artifacts/m10_subtitles_rtl.png); the font is
  the theme's, and lines_ar.csv stays empty.
- A `wreck` cuts off what was being said, and clear() does the same where
  the drive controller begins a Telling again.
- The two Subtitles settings of GDD 17.1 are in Settings and are applied
  the moment they change: `subtitle_size` (small, medium or large; medium)
  and `subtitle_background` (on). Sizes, margins, colours and the numbers
  of 16.6 are in data/tuning.json (subtitles_view).
- `--say=<line id>[,<line id>...]` asks for lines when the drive scene
  starts. The smoke test runs a line of two lines, an exchange and a line
  shown in parts (the test line subtitle.test.long, 143 characters: no
  line of GDD 3.6 is longer than two lines of 42).

tools/subtitles_check.gd checks all of it without a renderer and prints a
PASS or FAIL line for each of its 94 checks; it is not a step of
tools/check.sh. tools/subtitles_shots.sh takes the pictures:
artifacts/m10_subtitles_*.png.

In drive.tscn the Subtitles layer stands before the Overlay, so the
pointer is drawn over the subtitles; a PostFX layer belongs before it.

